t('reports/CIVICATION_SCENEKUNST_PROGRAM_OG_KURATERING_PREREQUISITES_SOURCE_FIRST.md',`# Civication — Scenekunst Program og kuratering prerequisites\n\n## Scope lock\n- Canonical key: \`${KEY}\`.\n- This is the source-first prerequisite package, **not Role World completion**.\n- Badge progression grants no employment, programming authority, contract power, financing or technical safety authority.\n- No new runtime system or global reputation score is introduced.\n\n## Persistent work and rhythm\nOne \`programportefolje_og_beslutningslogg\` persists across 16 steps: candidate, criteria, field research, habilitation, representation observations, rights, arena-fit, recommendation, decision owner, invitation/contract status and later effect. The loop is \`signal → research/kriterier → habilitet/rettigheter/representasjon/arena-fit → waiting → recommendation/decision → handoff → effect check → bounded rework\`. Changed premises reopen only affected fields.\n\n## Fictional work world\nFour fictional actors separate program authority (Leila), technical/safety feasibility (Tor), rights/agreement status (Mina) and field/representation research (Yusuf). Four surfaces separate portfolio criteria, field research, rights/agreements and arena-fit. Proposal, recommendation, decision, invitation, negotiation and signed booking remain different states.\n\n## Authored mail depth\nNine required mail types, **15 unique mails**: four job, four people and one each conflict, story, event, micro, follow-up, knowledge and consequence. The arc covers portfolio scarcity, rights, arena mismatch, handoff, mandate, technical refusal, contract language, narrow research, direct conflict of interest, representation criticism, a changed touring date, status language, bounded rework and a delayed informal-promise consequence. No generic fallbacks.\n\n## Functional History Go knowledge\nThe bounded task uses canonical \`inger_buresund\` at \`black_box_teater\` to ask how a programming theatre and artistic profile are built over time. It cannot prescribe today's program, prove artistic quality or grant habilitation, contract, budget, rights, safety or programming authority.\n\n## Cross-role boundary\nCross-role status remains \`not_required_for_rollout\`; no shared runtime object is materialized.\n\n## Verification\nThe strict gate proves appointment entry, manifest ownership, four fictional actors, four work surfaces, persistent work, waiting/handoff/rework, 15 authored mails, bounded History Go evidence, playable career state, removal of the four authored-work debts and preservation of \`not_required_for_rollout\`. The fail-closed workflow must pass focused testing, generated-state parity, full Civication and repository diff checks before permanent publication.\n\n## Six-part quality gate — 29/30\n| Dimension | Score | Evidence |\n| --- | ---: | --- |\n| Architecture and contracts | 5/5 | Program, habilitation, rights, agreement and technical mandates are separated. |\n| Content depth and specificity | 5/5 | One sustained 16-step portfolio case, four actors, four surfaces, 15 mails. |\n| State and consequence | 5/5 | Waiting, status language, bounded rework and delayed consequence. |\n| Test and generated-state integrity | 5/5 | Dedicated strict test plus canonical parity gates. |\n| Repository hygiene and scope | 5/5 | One role, one prerequisite package, no runtime expansion. |\n| Runtime evidence at publication | 4/5 | Exact-head PR CI supplies browser proof. |\n\nTotal: **29/30**. No critical prerequisite gap is accepted.`);
